            <ArticleTitle>Absence of human herpesvirus 8 genomes in coronary atherosclerosis in immunocompetent patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1245-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Human herpevirus 8 (HHV8) has been localized to the endothelial and spindle cells of KS, suggesting a role for HHV8 in atherosclerosis. None of the 38 coronary atherectomy specimens contained HHV8 with both sensitive nested PCR assays, making it unlikely that persistent viral infection with HHV8 plays a role in coronary atherogenesis in the general population of the United States.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
